rence gold tile has mottled surface variation; the candidate uses discrete flat randomly colored tile meshes and appears lighter and more uniform. /evidence/final_source/build.py:8-10,24-28; supplied images.", "For walnut floor the Generated coordinate output is multiplied by (2,28,3), passed through Noise scale 4 and a color ramp into the Principled Base Color; floor mesh is bound to that material. This produces stretched pattern in generated-coordinate space, not a direct measurement of physical grain alignment. /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-12,14-15,22; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1.", "The mirror has a metallic Principled material and two separate white rectangles simulating reflected cabinetry rather than reconstructing the detailed reference reflection. /evidence/final_source/build.py:58-63; original inventory:493-496; supplied images.", "No external image load is present in executed source; evaluator reports no missing external images. Source uses geometry and procedural materials, not a full-reference image plane. /evidence/executions/blender_1795841692942277709/code/build.py:1-80; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:7."],\n  "geometry_analysis": ["The front island countertop is a standalone slab at z 0.85-0.95, with no support created beneath it in the source, and appears floating in the delivered image. /evidence/final_source/build.py:68-71; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:503; supplied candidate image. This is an observable simplified structure, not an aligned GT error.", "The shelf bottom is at approximately z 0.278 and side bottoms at z 0.29, above the floor top z 0; its support is not shown in source. /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1,485-492. Bounding values do not alone establish physical support or collisions.", "Th