op with the bed, shelf and chair much larger in frame and a dark right foreground door. The candidate\'s chair is fully visible and the reference chair is cropped; the shelf and mattress overlap differ. These are 2D observations confounded by camera, layout and size, not aligned 3D errors. Camera parameters: /evidence/final_source/build.py:73-75.", "The bed headboard is at its left end and the shelf faces the room in the candidate; chair shell profile suggests a seat facing away from its raised back (/evidence/final_source/build.py:24-37,59-67). Hidden back faces and exact 3D orientation of the reference chair remain uncertain."],\n22\t  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["The reference shows a textured mattress side, streaked table and localized strong lamp illumination; the candidate mattress appears smooth, the table is simplified and overall lighting is flatter. These are observations of supplied reference and actual final capture, not a score.", "The script\'s mat function assigns constant Principled BSDF Base Color, Roughness and Metallic values; Table wood is assigned to Bedside table top, White mattress to Mattress, and Fine wood grain is separate Pale wood frame geometry (/evidence/final_source/build.py:6-14,32,39-45; original object_inventory.jsonl:49,56,61). No Texture Coordinate, Mapping, Noise, image texture or imported reference-image material is created in the executed source. Therefore procedural mapping direction/scale and packed image paths are not applicable to this authored material implementation; no full-reference image-plane shortcut is supported by the source.", "Original inspection reports no missing external images (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7). This does not itself prove that every possible packed resource was inspected. The reference\'s materials need not use the student\'s implementation."],\n23\t  "geometry_analysis": ["Shelf consists of seven vertical and five horizontal meshes (/evidence/final_source/build.py:24-27; original object_inventory.jsonl:32-43). Chair consists of a subdivided, solidified shell and four straight legs (/evidence/final_source/build.py:59-67; original object_inventory.jsonl:152-156); the reference\'s obscured support cannot be fully judged from the RGB.", "Original inventory places the four chair leg bottoms at z approximately 0.04, while the floor top is z 0; bed leg bottoms are approximately 0.03 and lamp bases approximately 0.02 (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1,45-48,144,148,153-156). These are student-scene world-bound indications of gaps relative to the floor, not full surface-contact or physical-stability tests; the rug may affect individual support relationships.", "No student door mesh or articulated hinge is constructed (/evidence/final_source/build.py:15-76). No collision or sweep test was recorded."],\n24\t  "semantic_correspondence": [\n25\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[19],"gt_semantic_label":"open cell shelf","student_object_names":["Shelf vertical","Shelf vertical.001","Shelf vertical.002","Shelf vertical.003","Shelf vertical.004","Shelf vertical.005","Shelf vertical.006","Shelf horizontal","Shelf horizontal.001","Shelf horizontal.002","Shelf horizontal.003","Shelf horizontal.004"],"confidence":"high","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:18-31", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:32-43", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:24-27"],"ambiguity":["Independent meshes form the shelf; camera and dimensions differ."],"orientation_identifiability":"Open front faces room; depth and hidden back are uncertain."},\n26\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[46],"gt_semantic_label":"mattress","student_object_names":["Mattress","Mattress piping","Mattress piping.001"],"confidence":"high","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:106-119", "/evidence/independen