or recovery is recorded (/evidence/sdk_events.json:90-107; /evidence/evidence_index.json:135-150)."],\n  "side_effects": ["The doorway is a black slab over an uninterrupted tiled back wall, rather than a cut opening; the leaf has no parent pivot (/evidence/final_source/build.py:20-26,60-63; original object_inventory.jsonl:556-558). The simulated reflected cupboard consists of physical boxes in front of the mirror, not just a reflection (/evidence/final_source/build.py:52-59; original object_inventory.jsonl:545-555)."],\n  "spatial_and_orientation_analysis": ["The reference and final image both show the left dark appliance, central range, small shelf behind/right, right white counter and foreground dark top. However the candidate is framed farther back: floor and island front are much more visible, the right cabinet is not cropped as in the reference, and appliances occupy a smaller image area (reference image; /evidence/executions/blender_1795841573989638875/artifacts/final.png). Camera, layout, scale and perspective are confounded; no aligned world errors are justified.", "The appliance fronts face the viewer and the range burners face upward in both images; exact orientation, concealed rear geometry and absolute scale remain uncertain. The reference doorway is bright and partly occluded by a broad brown leaf, while the student has a narrow dark slit and thin leaf (same images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:60-63). The candidate\'s 35 mm perspective camera and geometry do not establish a common frame with GT (/evidence/independent_evaluation/common_light/capture/common_light_settings.json:189-227; /evidence/reference_gt/common_light/capture/common_light_settings.json:248-286)."],\n  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["The reference wall has mottled dark gold tiles, the student wall has more uniform small gold squares; the reference countertop has visible streaking whereas the candidate\'s appears nearly uniform (reference and /evidence/executions/blender_1795841573989638875/artifacts/final.png).", "The assigned walnut plank floor material connects Generated coordinates to Vector Math MULTIPLY (2,30,3), then Noise Fac to ColorRamp and Principled Base Color; box applies scale before assignment (/evidence/final_source/build.py:9-10,16-18). The white marble countertop has Noise Fac to ColorRamp to Principled Base Color with no explicit vector connection; it is bound to marble counter (/evidence/final_source/build.py:65-67; original object_inventory.jsonl:559-560). Default node output connection is used, not a separately implemented image map.", "No image resources are referenced by the delivered source and the evaluator reports no missing external images (/evidence/final_source/build.py:1-79; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7). A full-reference image-plane replacement is unsupported; scene inventory and source instead show separately modeled meshes. Packed-image status was not independently established."],\n  "geometry_analysis": ["The foreground island box spans z=0.26 to 1.02 while the floor top is z=0, so its body floats above the floor in the actual scene; top overlaps the box slightly (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1,562-563). Reference foreground lower structure is occluded, so its support is not identifiable.", "The back wall and tiles remain across the doorway, so the apparent opening is not structural (/evidence/final_source/build.py:20-26,60-63). Evaluator reported 185 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections or contact (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-16)."],\n  "semantic_correspondence": [\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [60], "gt_semantic_label": "oven and electric range", "student_object_names": ["range body", "range stainless cooktop", "round electric burner", "round electric burner.001", "round electric burner.002", "round electric burner.