76). The wallpaper is actual beveled spline geometry using \'fine hexagon outlines\', not an image texture or directional-mapping network (lines 24-35). No texture-coordinate or image mapping is created by this source. Independent summary reports no missing external images (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-8); packed resources are not independently established. No evidence of a full-reference image plane appears in the source or original inventory.", "Independent common-light images are auxiliary evaluator renders, not student observations: /evidence/independent_evaluation/common_light/capture/common_light.png and /evidence/reference_gt/common_light/capture/common_light.png. The GT auxiliary is very dark and noisy while the student is light; remaining camera, material, emission and lighting confounds preclude attributing the difference to material improvement (/app/input_index.json:24-29)."],\n20\t  "geometry_analysis": ["The script creates separate desk tops and four legs, chair seat/back, central support, five spokes and five caster meshes, and separate lamp parts (/evidence/final_source/build.py:43-79); these are editable but not parented assemblies in original inventory. Apparent contact cannot be established from bounds or a single render. The wall is a solid cube behind the window panes rather than a cut opening (/evidence/final_source/build.py:20,37-41); the panes visually represent a window but do not establish a through-wall opening.", "Original inspection reports 270 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-16). Hidden support and physical clearances remain uncertain."],\n21\t  "semantic_correspondence": [\n22\t    {"gt_instance_ids": [63], "gt_semantic_label": "floor", "student_object_names": ["floor"], "confidence": "high", "basis": ["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:898-911 identif