eces, repeated desks, parametric chair shells and casters, lamps, lights and a directly aimed camera; saves and renders. Capture stdout.log:1-5 and original object_inventory.jsonl:1-194 corroborate reached output.", "The helper line() is defined at /evidence/final_source/build.py:14-17 but has no call in the source; do not credit its execution."],\n  "student_verification": ["The student ran Blender once and received save/render log output (SDK events 3 and 5, tool call call-403d60ea43ac48cbaa980161e0043abb). No image-open tool call, visual comparison, alternate view, projections, revision, swatch, or structural audit is recorded in events 0-6. The rendered image exists, but the trace does not show the student inspecting it."],\n  "failures_and_recovery": ["Delivery is complete: build.py, scene.blend and final.png exist (/app/input_index.json:8-15). SDK ended successfully with no recorded model errors (/evidence/evidence_index.json:29-35,43-45,53-60); no SDK/Bridge failure is recorded. Blender execution exit 0 and capture log show save and render, with no captured traceback (/evidence/evidence_index.json:120-150). Deprecation warnings for Material.use_nodes and World.use_nodes occurred (SDK event 5); no recovery or revision recorded."],\n  "side_effects": ["Source removes initial scene objects (/evidence/final_source/build.py:3), then creates 194 scene objects including 186 meshes according to independent original summary:2-8. The duplicated right wallpaper curve is transformed away from the right wall: original object_inventory.jsonl:3,7 reports separated world bounds; this is a retained spatial side effect, not a proven cause of all visual differences."],\n  "spatial_and_orientation_analysis": ["The reference and delivered image show repeated white swivel chairs facing desks, a rear two-pane window, and two right-side lamps. Reference foreground chairs are larger and the desk rows recede obliquely; the candidate is more frontal, with a smaller window and more uniformly scaled, horizontally aligned furniture. The far-right candidate chair is cropped. Camera, lens and layout jointly affect these differences; no aligned 3D error follows (reference and delivered images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:43-48,50-72,83).", "Foreground chair backs face the camera and the scripted local forward is +Y; two chairs have nonzero yaw (/evidence/final_source/build.py:50-53,72). Exact reference yaw, hidden depth, and symmetry-ambiguous chair base orientation are not identifiable from the image. Chair/desk occlusions support only visible depth order; do not infer unique distances.", "The narrow dark cabinet at reference right edge (GT instance 125, /evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:482-495) has no clear modeled counterpart in original inventory; framing also differs."],\n  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["Reference and candidate both show pale walls and floor, dark desks, white chairs and honeycomb wall lines, but the delivered render has weaker localized lamp glow, a flatter, brighter appearance and less prominent furniture than the reference (actual reference and delivered final images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:74-85).", "Student mat() sets Base Color, Roughness and Metallic on the default Principled material; materials are bound by cube/cyl and chair/lamp creation (/evidence/final_source/build.py:5-13,55-76). The wallpaper is actual beveled spline geometry using \'fine hexagon outlines\', not an image texture or directional-mapping network (lines 24-35). No texture-coordinate or image mapping is created by this source. Independent summary reports no missing external images (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-8); packed resources are not independently established. No evidence of a full-reference image plane appears in the source or original inventory.", "Independent common-light images are auxiliary evaluator renders, not student observations: /evidence/independent_evaluation/common_light/capture/common_light.png and /evidence/reference_gt/common_light/capture/common_light.png. The GT auxiliary is very dark and noisy while the student is light; remaining camera, material, emission and lighting confounds preclude attributing the difference to material improvement (/app/input_index.json:24-29)."],\n  "geometry_analysis": ["The script creates separate desk tops and four legs, chair seat/back, central support, five spokes and five caster meshes, and separate lamp parts (/evidence/final_source/build.py:43-79); these are editable but not parented assemblies in original inventory. Apparent contact cannot be established from bounds or a single render. The wall is a solid cube behind the window panes rather than a cut opening (/evidence/final_source/build.py:20,37-41); the panes visually represent a window but do not establish a through-wall opening.", "Original inspection reports 270 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-16). Hidden support and physical clearances remain uncertain."],\n  "semantic_correspondence": [\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [63], "gt_semantic_label": "floor", "student_object_names": ["floor"], "confidence": "high", "basis": ["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:898-911 identifies visible floor", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1"], "ambiguity": ["Projection and extent differ; correspondence is semantic, not measured alignment."], "orientation_identifiability": "Horizontal floor plane is identifiable; in-plane rotation is not."},\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [67], "gt_semantic_label": "room wall", "student_object_names": ["back wall", "right wall"], "confidence": "medium", "basis": ["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:922-935", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inv