2026-11-28 05:32:23,423 - INFO - [MainThread] - Received claude code message: {'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call-8ee6e645f1ed43b393b7f4c39b027aef', 'content': '1\t{\n2\t  "annotation_kind": "automated_model",\n3\t  "overall_fidelity_estimate_0_100": 61,\n4\t  "scene_description": "Both images show a small pale room viewed from above, with a light blue three-seat sofa and right-hand chaise against the back wall, a framed wall picture to the left, a mirror above the sofa, a floor lamp and white cabinet to its right, a low white unit to the left, and a coffee table in front. The reference additionally shows a prominent open wood shelving unit on the right and a pale round rug; these are not comparably visible in the candidate.",\n5\t  "visible_objects": {\n6\t    "observations": "The principal furniture arrangement is recognizable in both images. The candidate\'s large right foreground object is a plain pale face rather than the reference\'s open, wood-grained cubby shelving. The candidate artwork has a dark central shape rather than the reference\'s colorful land-like shapes.",\n7\t    "image_evidence": "Reference: sofa [0.24, 0.26, 0.66, 0.66], shelves [0.71, 0.00, 1.00, 1.00]. Candidate: sofa [0.29, 0.31, 0.67, 0.65], right foreground face [0.76, 0.02, 1.00, 1.00]. Regions are normalized."\n8\t  },\n9\t  "spatial_relations_and_orientation": {\n10\t    "observations": "Both place the sofa at the back with its chaise extending toward the viewer on the right; the mirror is above it, lamp and tall cabinet to the right, low unit to the left, and coffee table in front. The candidate shows more empty floor between sofa and table and presents the wall art more fully, while the right foreground object obscures much of that side.",\n11\t    "image_evidence": "Reference sofa and table [0.24, 0.26, 0.67, 1.00]; candidate sofa and table [0.29, 0.31, 0.67, 1.00]."\n12\t  },\n13\t  "proportions_and_occlusion": {\n14\t    "observations": "The candidate sofa occupies less image width and height than the reference sofa. Its table is fully visible across its top and smaller in frame; the reference tabletop is substantially cropped by the bottom edge. The candidate right object reads as an uninterrupted slab, unlike the reference\'s visibly subdivided shelves. The reference rug is broad and visible around the table; no comparably distinct circular rug is evident in the candidate.",\n15\t    "image_evidence": "Reference sofa [0.24, 0.26, 0.66, 0.66], tabletop [0.38, 0.66, 0.67, 1.00]; candidate sofa [0.29, 0.31, 0.67, 0.65], tabletop [0.38, 0.71, 0.64, 0.93]."\n16\t  },\n17\t  "materials_and_texture": {\n18\t    "observations": "Both sofas are pale cyan and softly shaded. Reference shelving has warm light wood grain and repeated open compartments; the candidate foreground face is smooth and near-monochrome. The reference tabletop has broad diagonal brown and white streaks, whereas the candidate uses thin, evenly spaced white diagonal lines on a muted brown surface. The reference wall art is predominantly dark blue with salmon and yellow shapes; the candidate has a pale purple field and a stark black shape with a pink surround.",\n19\t    "image_evidence": "Reference shelves [0.71, 0.00, 1.00, 1.00], table [0.38, 0.66, 0.67, 1.00], art [0.00, 0.00, 0.22, 0.53]; candidate corresponding right face [0.76, 0.02, 1.00, 1.00], table [0.38, 0.71, 0.64, 0.93], art [0.06, 0.06, 0.22, 0.52]."\n20\t  },\n21\t  "visible_geometry": {\n22\t    "observations": "Both sofas show three back cushions, three seat sections, arms, and a right projecting chaise. Candidate cushions are more box-like and segmented, and the chaise legs are exposed. Reference shelving has thick vertical and horizontal dividers and deep open bays; these connections are absent from the visible candidate face. Both tables are rectangular, but their top patterns and framing differ.",\n23\t    "image_evidence": "Reference sofa [0.24, 0.26, 0.66, 0.66] and shelves [0.71, 0.00, 1.00, 1.00]; candida