ity":"minor","priority":"low","confidence":"high"},\n    {"object":"floor lamp and white cabinet","region":[0.63,0.12,0.80,0.68],"observation":"Both are at the right end of the sofa. Their general placement is retained, although they occupy a smaller portion of the candidate frame.","evidence_image":"reference; candidate comparison [0.59,0.27,0.71,0.58]","severity":"minor","priority":"low","confidence":"high"},\n    {"object":"round rug","region":[0.20,0.59,0.78,1.00],"observation":"The reference rug appears pale pink and is substantially cropped; the candidate rug is nearly white and its circular outline is more visible.","evidence_image":"reference; candidate comparison [0.30,0.57,0.72,0.99]","severity":"minor","priority":"medium","confidence":"medium"}\n  ],\n  "most_important_visible_defects": [\n    "The camera framing is markedly wider and less close than the reference, changing the apparent scale and cropping of nearly every object.",\n    "The right shelving loses much of the reference\'s warm wood grain and dominant foreground presence.",\n    "The coffee table\'s finer stripe pattern and dark wedge differ noticeably from the broad reflective reference streaks.",\n    "Sofa cushions are more boxy and the chaise appears less substantial; the artwork\'s color and framing also differ."\n  ],\n  "uncertainty": "The back-wall rectangle may be a mirror or a framed image; its precise function is not established. Apparent size differences can result from camera placement or field of view rather than actual object dimensions. Exact contact, hidden surfaces, physical scale and symmetry cannot be established from these images alone.",\n  "limitations": "Evaluation is based only on the two supplied RGB images, using approximate normalized image coordinates. Bright exposure and occlusion limit assessment of fine material properties, geometry and shadows. No unseen surfaces or underlying implementation were evaluated.",\n  "human_rating": null\n}\n', 'numLines': 53, 'sta