ar parallel tabletop stripes. These are visible comparisons, not causal isolation of lighting and material. Evidence: provided reference and candidate; /evidence/final_source/build.py:40-42,47-59,91-95.", "The authored mat function sets constant Principled Base Color, Roughness and Metallic and does not construct texture, mapping or image nodes (/evidence/final_source/build.py:6-8). Wood grain uses rotated pale mesh strips, not texture coordinates (/evidence/final_source/build.py:50-53). No image-loading or packing operation is present in the delivered source; evaluator original summary reports no missing external images (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7). The source creates object geometry rather than a full-reference image plane (/evidence/final_source/build.py:19-89)."],\n18\t  "geometry_analysis": ["The cubby is assembled from intersecting horizontal shelves and continuous uprights; dark joint marks are visible in the candidate. The student\'s chair is a single subdivided solidified shell with four rods, not an established swivel mechanism (/evidence/final_source/build.py:30-34,73-84). The door is a narrow unparented block without a hinge assembly (/evidence/final_source/build.py:88-89; original object inventory:168).", "Evaluator inventory places mattress bounds at z=0.36-0.74 and platform at z=0.20-0.40, so their bounding boxes overlap; this is broad-phase evidence only, not proof of an unintended mesh intersection (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:46-51). The evaluator\'s 553 AABB overlap candidates are not confirmed collisions (/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8)."],\n19\t  "semantic_correspondence": [\n20\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[19],"gt_semantic_label":"open cubby shelf","student_object_names":["Bookcase side","Bookcase side.001","Bookcase horizontal shelf","Bookcase horizontal shelf.001","Bookc