2026-11-28 05:32:55,595 - INFO - [MainThread] - Received claude code message: {'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call-7dc4b55ee4bb4c6c8b35cd75f28016c2', 'content': '1\t{\n2\t  "annotation_kind": "automated_model",\n3\t  "run_id": "A-T03-A0",\n4\t  "scene_id": "A-T03",\n5\t  "capability_availability": {\n6\t    "public_library": "none",\n7\t    "knowledge_present_in_initial_context": false,\n8\t    "evidence": ["/app/input_index.json:32", "/evidence/student_initial_prompt.txt:1-18", "/evidence/initial_model_input.json:1", "/evidence/evidence_index.json:21-25"]\n9\t  },\n10\t  "adoption": [\n11\t    {\n12\t      "unit": "Student-authored procedural geometry and material helpers",\n13\t      "module": "final_source/build.py",\n14\t      "function": "mat, cube, cyl, area",\n15\t      "provenance_category": "unknown",\n16\t      "phases": {"read": false, "written": true, "executed": true, "verified": false, "retained": true},\n17\t      "actual_call_evidence": ["/evidence/sdk_events.json events 1, 2 and 5, tool IDs call-ea9419e902ee4a1fb14162b0d312858c and call-ee6ed41c64b648d1b88d539e9fd8f276", "/evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/code/build.py:6-17,19-83", "/evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stdout.log:1-5", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482,547-549"],\n18\t      "modified_or_inlined": "Helpers are defined directly in the student\'s source; no library citation or library origin is evidenced.",\n19\t      "observed_outcome": "The executed source created meshes, materials and lights, saved the scene and rendered an image; the source and these scene objects were retained.",\n20\t      "attribution_uncertainty": "Ordinary similarities to other methods cannot establish provenance or benefit. No optional library was supplied. Successful output is not a student visual verification."\n21\t    }\n22\t  ],\n23\t  "nonuse": ["No public capability library or SKILL.md was supplied in this base condition; the initial request and complete SDK trace show no library read, import or invocation. This is nonuse of an unavailable optional resource, not a failure to use a required library. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:32; /evidence/student_initial_prompt.txt:1-18; /evidence/initial_model_input.json:1; /evidence/sdk_events.json:1-191."],\n24\t  "methods_actually_executed": [\n25\t    "The student wrote /app/build.py and ran Blender once with -b -t 8 --python /app/build.py; the separate Blender --version call was not a reconstruction execution. Evidence: /evidence/sdk_events.json events 0-5; /evidence/evidence_index.json:120-168.",\n26\t    "Reached source uses seeded random tile materials, cube and cylinder primitives, optional bevel and weighted-normal modifiers, a procedural floor, two area lights, a perspective camera, Cycles rendering, and save/render operations. Evidence: /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/code/build.py:3-83; stdout.log:1-5; original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1-12,467-549 under /evidence/independent_evaluation."\n27\t  ],\n28\t  "student_verification": ["The student received a successful Blender tool result reporting both saved files, but the trace contains no image Read, scene inspection, visual comparison, or revision after rendering. Evidence: /evidence/sdk_events.json events 2, 5 and 6; /evidence/evidence_index.json:116-168."],\n29\t  "failures_and_recovery": ["The actual build completed with exit code 0, saved scene.blend and final.png, and its capture lists no Python traceback. A Material.use_nodes deprecation warning was emitted; no recovery was required or recorded. Evidence: /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stderr.log:1-2; /evidence/evidence_index.json:140-168.", "All requested artifacts were delivered and SDK status was completed with success; no SDK or Bridge failure is recorded for the student run. The unrelated image-reading diagnostic in the annotation invocation is not evidence of a student-run failure. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:8-16; /evidence/evidence_index.json:3-5,30-35,43-45,53-60,104-109; /evidence/sdk_events.json:143-190."],\n30\t  "side_effects": ["The executed script deletes initially selected scene objects before constructing the scene and saves /app/scene.blend and /app/final.png; these are in the student\'s workspace. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:4,81-83; /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stdout.log:1-2.", "The mirror representation places two white cabinet meshes immediately in front of its reflective surface, so they are modeled stand-ins rather than solely physical reflections. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:53-58; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:526-529."],\n31\t  "spatial_and_orientation_analysis": ["Both actual images show a range with a dark appliance to its left and a white cubby to its right, a tiled back wall, a mirror above left, a right-side counter and a dark foreground surface. Evidence: supplied reference image and actual candidate final image; /evidence/final_source/build.py:18-74.", "The reconstruction frames the room much farther back: the entire upper edge of the back wall and surrounding dark exterior are visible, appliances occupy less of the frame, and the foreground island reads as a large left-hand block. The reference is a tighter interior view with strong foreground cropping and a larger oven and left appliance. These image differences combine camera, geometry, layout and occlusion; their individual causes are not isolated. Evidence: supplied reference and final images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:73-81.", "The range and left appliance fronts face the student\'s negative Y direction, with the hotplates horizontal. The student\'s door is an axis-aligned panel despite its \'open\' name; its reference hinge angle is not reliably recoverable from one view. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:26-47,59-63; original inventory lines 468-482 and 530-535; supplied reference image.", "No world-position, rotation, scale error or mask score is asserted because GT and student coordinates are not registered and the scene is visible from only one reference viewpoint. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:21-33; /evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:458."\n32\t  ],\n33\t  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["Compared with the reference, the delivered image has paler, regular solid-color tiles rather than dark mottled tiles; the white counter appears mostly plain, and the dark left appliance has a prominent front grid. The mirror shows simplified white rectangles rather than the reference\'s detailed reflected cabinetry. Evidence: supplied actual reference and candidate images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:8-11,39-47,53-58,64-66.", "The \'dark wood floor\' material is assigned to mesh \'floor\'. Its authored node chain is Generated coordinates -> Mapping scale (3,35,3) -> Noise Texture (scale 4, detail 3) -> ColorRamp -> Principled BSDF Base Color. This is procedural directional variation, not an image texture; the shader output connection is Blender\'s default material setup and was not separately established from a material-state link record. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-7,10-11,19; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1.", "The material called \'white trim\', not a marble texture, is assigned to \'right white marble countertop\'; the dark smoky glass and brushed stainless names describe Principled parameters, not verified physical glass or brushed microstructure. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-8,65-66; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:469-470,475,537.", "The source does not load an image texture or reference image into the scene; evaluator summary reports no missing external images, but this alone does not establish packed-resource details. No full-reference image-plane replacement is evidenced. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:1-83; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7."\n34\t  ],\n35\t  "geometry_analysis": ["The delivered scene is constructed from separate cuboids and cylinders, including physically volumetric appliance bodies, shelf panels and tiles; many front details are thin surface-mounted pieces. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:12-74; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482,519-537.", "The evaluator reported 634 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections or defects. Intended contacts and nested parts can produce such candidates; no exact penetration claim is made. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-16.", "Doorway darkness is a dark thin box placed in front of a continuous back wall, rather than evidence of a cut opening, and reflected cabinets are stand-in geometry. This is structurally simpler than a fully modeled adjoining room. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:20,53-63; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:2,526-535."\n36\t  ],\n37\t  "semantic_correspondence": [\n38\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[60],"gt_semantic_label":"oven","student_object_names":["range body","oven front","oven glass","oven bottom lip","oven handle","handle mounting","handle mounting.001","cooktop","electric hotplate","electric hotplate.001","electric hotplate.002","electric hotplate.003","raised control panel","range control dial","range control dial.001"],"confidence":"high","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:193-207", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:26-38", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482"],"ambiguity":["Proposed assembly membership and mask alignment are not manually verified."],"orientation_identifiability":"Front and top are visually identifiable; exact 3D angle remains unregistered."},\n39\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[13],"gt_semantic_label":"cell_shelf","student_object_names":["shelf back","shelf upright","shelf upright.001","shelf upright.002","shelf horizontal","shelf horizontal.001","shelf horizontal.002"],"confidence":"high","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:50-64", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:48-52", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:519-525"],"ambiguity":["Lower shelf is partly obscured in the reference."],"orientation_identifiability":"Open front is visible; depth and precise rotation are uncertain."},\n40\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[54],"gt_semantic_label":"mirror","student_object_names":["mirror dark frame","mirror glass","reflected upper cabinet","reflected upper cabinet.001"],"confidence":"medium","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:162-176", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:53-58", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:526-529"],"ambiguity":["The two foreground white meshes imitate reflected content and may need separate treatment in a mask protocol."],"orientation_identifiability":"Vertical wall placement is visible; mirror-normal angle is uncertain."},\n41\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[23],"gt_semantic_label":"dishwasher","student_object_names":["wine fridge black housing","wine cooler glass door","wine cooler top rail","wine cooler handle","wine rack shelf","wine rack shelf.001","wine rack shelf.002","wine rack shelf.003"],"confidence":"medium","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:98-112", "/evidence/reference_gt/objects_in_view.json:29-34", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:39-47", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:483-486,494,502,510,518"],"ambiguity":["GT class is dishwasher although the student labeled its left-hand visual counterpart a wine cooler; the listed meshes omit individual grid bars, so this is an incomplete assembly proposal."],"orientation_identifiability":"Front and top visible, exact angle not established."},\n42\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[5],"gt_semantic_label":"beverage_fridge","student_object_names":["dark island top","foreground island"],"confidence":"medium","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:25-40", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:72-74", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:545-546"],"ambiguity":["The visible GT region is a cropped dark foreground surface; the student modeled an island, so object identity and hidden form differ."],"orientation_identifiability":"Only top-plane orientation is partly visible; hidden front and exact rotation are unknown."},\n43\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[42],"gt_semantic_label":"kitchen_space","student_object_names":["right base cabinets","right white marble countertop","cabinet door seam","cabinet door seam.001","cabinet door seam.002","cabinet handle","cabinet handle.001","cabinet handle.002","upper cabinet"],"confidence":"medium","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:113-128", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:64-71", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:536-544"],"ambiguity":["GT kitchen-space asset may include a different assembly partition; portions are cropped or occluded."],"orientation_identifiability":"Counter long axis is visually discernible; exact angle and hidden cabinetry are uncertain."},\n44\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[26],"gt_semantic_label":"panel_door","student_object_names":["dark open door","door inset panel","door inset panel.001","door inset panel.002"],"confidence":"medium","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/refere