nly/reproduction.json:1-17,25-42.", "Common-white-world student and GT images/settings are evaluator-only. They hide existing lights and change world and render settings while retaining geometry, material, camera, and possible emission confounds; no material-improvement claim is inferred. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:24-29; /evidence/independent_evaluation/common_light/capture/common_light_settings.json:108-186,930-939; /evidence/reference_gt/common_light/capture/common_light_settings.json:155-245,1925-1934."\n49\t  ],\n50\t  "unsupported_or_unknown_claims": ["No hidden reasoning, general knowledge acquisition, library-derived benefit, visual score, numerical alignment or mask error is established. Evidence: /evidence/sdk_events.json:1-191; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:10-15.", "The GT wall instance and the hundreds of independent tile meshes have no complete explicitly enumerated correspondence here; the cropped GT single cabinet and two-pixel plant container likewise have no reliable student match. Evidence: /evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:138-152,234-264,394-408; /evidence/final_source/build.py:18-25,64-74."],\n51\t  "limitations": ["All semantic correspondences are model-proposed, incomplete where stated, and have not been manually verified; they require deterministic validation before projection-mask use.", "Original inventory projected bounds are unclipped, bottom-up object bounding boxes, not visible-mask centroids. GT masks do not establish hidden geometry or pairwise depth order. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:15; /evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:458.", "The attached actual delivered candidate and reference support qualitative visual observations; evaluator auxiliary images were not visually inspected for this annotation, so no auxiliary appearance conclusion is asserted. No human rating was supplied."],\n52\t  "human_rating": null\n53\t}\n54\t', 'is_error': None}], 'uuid': '457524fd-96e5-439e-8756-2de06aecf970', 'parent_tool_use_id': None, 'tool_use_result': {'type': 'text', 'file': {'filePath': '/reviews/A-T03-A0/technical_annotation.json', 'content': '{\n  "annotation_kind": "automated_model",\n  "run_id": "A-T03-A0",\n  "scene_id": "A-T03",\n  "capability_availability": {\n    "public_library": "none",\n    "knowledge_present_in_initial_context": false,\n    "evidence": ["/app/input_index.json:32", "/evidence/student_initial_prompt.txt:1-18", "/evidence/initial_model_input.json:1", "/evidence/evidence_index.json:21-25"]\n  },\n  "adoption": [\n    {\n      "unit": "Student-authored procedural geometry and material helpers",\n      "module": "final_source/build.py",\n      "function": "mat, cube, cyl, area",\n      "provenance_category": "unknown",\n      "phases": {"read": false, "written": true, "executed": true, "verified": false, "retained": true},\n      "actual_call_evidence": ["/evidence/sdk_events.json events 1, 2 and 5, tool IDs call-ea9419e902ee4a1fb14162b0d312858c and call-ee6ed41c64b648d1b88d539e9fd8f276", "/evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/code/build.py:6-17,19-83", "/evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stdout.log:1-5", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482,547-549"],\n      "modified_or_inlined": "Helpers are defined directly in the student\'s source; no library citation or library origin is evidenced.",\n      "observed_outcome": "The executed source created meshes, materials and lights, saved the scene and rendered an image; the source and these scene objects were retained.",\n      "attribution_uncertainty": "Ordinary similarities to other methods cannot establish provenance or benefit. No optional library was supplied. Successful output is not a student visual verification."\n    }\n  ],\n  "nonuse": ["No public capability library or SKILL.md was supplied in this base condition; the initial request and complete SDK trace show no library read, import or invocation. This is nonuse of an unavailable optional resource, not a failure to use a required library. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:32; /evidence/student_initial_prompt.txt:1-18; /evidence/initial_model_input.json:1; /evidence/sdk_events.json:1-191."],\n  "methods_actually_executed": [\n    "The student wrote /app/build.py and ran Blender once with -b -t 8 --python /app/build.py; the separate Blender --version call was not a reconstruction execution. Evidence: /evidence/sdk_events.json events 0-5; /evidence/evidence_index.json:120-168.",\n    "Reached source uses seeded random tile materials, cube and cylinder primitives, optional bevel and weighted-normal modifiers, a procedural floor, two area lights, a perspective camera, Cycles rendering, and save/render operations. Evidence: /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/code/build.py:3-83; stdout.log:1-5; original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1-12,467-549 under /evidence/independent_evaluation."\n  ],\n  "student_verification": ["The student received a successful Blender tool result reporting both saved files, but the trace contains no image Read, scene inspection, visual comparison, or revision after rendering. Evidence: /evidence/sdk_events.json events 2, 5 and 6; /evidence/evidence_index.json:116-168."],\n  "failures_and_recovery": ["The actual build completed with exit code 0, saved scene.blend and final.png, and its capture lists no Python traceback. A Material.use_nodes deprecation warning was emitted; no recovery was required or recorded. Evidence: /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stderr.log:1-2; /evidence/evidence_index.json:140-168.", "All requested artifacts were delivered and SDK status was completed with success; no SDK or Bridge failure is recorded for the student run. The unrelated image-reading diagnostic in the annotation invocation is not evidence of a student-run failure. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:8-16; /evidence/evidence_index.json:3-5,30-35,43-45,53-60,104-109; /evidence/sdk_events.json:143-190."],\n  "side_effects": ["The executed script deletes initially selected scene objects before constructing the scene and saves /app/scene.blend and /app/final.png; these are in the student\'s workspace. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:4,81-83; /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stdout.log:1-2.", "The mirror representation places two white cabinet meshes immediately in front of its reflective surface, so they are modeled stand-ins rather than solely physical reflections. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:53-58; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:526-529."],\n  "spatial_and_orientation_analysis": ["Both actual images show a range with a dark appliance to its left and a white cubby to its right, a tiled back wall, a mirror above left, a right-side counter and a dark foreground surface. Evidence: supplied reference image and actual candidate final image; /evidence/final_source/build.py:18-74.", "The reconstruction frames the room much farther back: the entire upper edge of the back wall and surrounding dark exterior are visible, appliances occupy less of the frame, and the foreground island reads as a large left-hand block. The reference is a tighter interior view with strong foreground cropping and a larger oven and left appliance. These image differences combine camera, geometry, layout and occlusion; their individual causes are not isolated. Evidence: supplied reference and final images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:73-81.", "The range and left appliance fronts face the student\'s negative Y direction, with the hotplates horizontal. The student\'s door is an axis-aligned panel despite its \'open\' name; its reference hinge angle is not reliably recoverable from one view. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:26-47,59-63; original inventory lines 468-482 and 530-535; supplied reference image.", "No world-position, rotation, scale error or mask score is asserted because GT and student coordinates are not registered and the scene is visible from only one reference viewpoint. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:21-33; /evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:458."\n  ],\n  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["Compared with the reference, the delivered image has paler, regular solid-color tiles rather than dark mottled tiles; the white counter appears mostly plain, and the dark left appliance has a prominent front grid. The mirror shows simplified white rectangles rather than the reference\'s detailed reflected cabinetry. Evidence: supplied actual reference and candidate images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:8-11,39-47,53-58,64-66.", "The \'dark wood floor\' material is assigned to mesh \'floor\'. Its authored node chain is Generated coordinates -> Mapping scale (3,35,3) -> Noise Texture (scale 4, detail 3) -> ColorRamp -> Principled BSDF Base Color. This is procedural directional variation, not an image texture; the shader output connection is Blender\'s default material setup and was not separately established from a material-state link record. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-7,10-11,19; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1.", "The material called \'white trim\', not a marble texture, is assigned to \'right white marble countertop\'; the dark smoky glass and brushed stainless names describe Principled parameters, not verified physical glass or brushed microstructure. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-8,65-66; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:469-470,475,537.", "The source does not load an image texture or reference image into the scene; evaluator summary reports no missing external images, but this alone does not establish packed-resource details. No full-reference image-plane replacement is evidenced. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:1-83; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7."\n  ],\n  "geometry_analysis": ["The delivered scene is constructed from separate cuboids and cylinders, including physically volumetric appliance bodies, shelf panels and tiles; many front details are thin surface-mounted pieces. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:12-74; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482,519-537.", "The evaluator reported 634 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections or defects. Intended contacts and nested parts can produce such candidates; no exact penetration claim is made. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-16.", "Doorway darkness is a dark thin box placed in front of a continuous back wall, rather than evidence of a cut opening, and reflected cabinets are stand-in geometry. This is structurally simpler than a fully modeled adjoining room. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:20,53-63; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:2,526-535."\n  ],\n  "semantic_correspondence": [\n    {"gt_instance_ids":[60],"gt_semantic_label":"oven","student_object_names":["range body","oven front","oven glass","oven bottom lip","oven handle","handle mounting","handle mounting.001","cooktop","electric hotplate","electric hotplate.001","electric hotplate.002","electric hotplate.003","raised control panel","range control dial","range control dial.001"],"confidence":"high","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:193-207", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:26-38", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482"],"ambiguity":["Proposed assembly membership and mask alignm